# Summary: Pi artifact commands

Artifacts are files a pi session saves outside the git repo so they survive
across sessions (see `dotfiles/pi/.pi/agent/extensions/artifacts.ts`).

These commands own the storage model. The extension asks `dev artifacts dir`
rather than deriving the location, so a pi session, a shell, and the `prefix e`
picker cannot disagree about where a project's artifacts live. They used to,
because the base was `$TMPDIR`: the tmux server, a login shell, and a pi session
started from either had different values for it, and a session was told its
artifacts did not exist.

The filesystem is the source of truth:

    $XDG_STATE_HOME/pi-artifacts/<hash>/     default ~/.local/state
      <slug>.<ext>     the artifacts
      .index.json      optional sidecar with a title and type per file

`<hash>` is the first 16 hex characters of the sha256 of the project root (git
top-level, falling back to the given path). The sidecar only enriches a
listing; the set of artifacts is whatever non-dotfiles exist in the directory.

A project that has never saved an artifact has no directory, so its absence is
normal and every command here treats it as an empty project. Nothing prunes the
base directory: it survives reboots now, and a project directory outlives the
checkout it was named after.
